#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Tanga: German East Africa, 4 November 1914.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

Eight thousand men of Indian Expeditionary Force B have come ashore at
Ras Kasone to take the port of Tanga, the end of the railway into the
highlands.  Paul von Lettow-Vorbeck has a thousand askari and a few
hundred German settlers, and more coming down the line by train.
Between the beach and the town lie rubber plantations and thick bush,
and in the trees there are wild bees.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./tanga (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.tanga.json.  ./tanga --selftest checks the map and plays a
game between two computer players.
"""

